# Development values only. Nothing here is a secret.
# The environment of `make migrate` and `make api` on the host, and of the containers `migrate` and
# `api` of docker-compose.app.yml. Those containers share one network namespace, so 127.0.0.1
# means the same there. The file holds the database URL, the API URL and the path of the service
# configuration. The API reads every other setting from huron.dev.yaml, the one file to edit. A
# HURON_* variable added here wins over that file, so add one only to override it.
# The API has no setting HURON_API_URL and does not read it. The CLI reads HURON_API_URL as its own
# setting, so never load this file into the environment of the CLI.
HURON_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://huron:huron@127.0.0.1:5432/huron
HURON_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080
# The service configuration, with the declared organizations: relative to the repository root for
# `make api`; the API container of `make app` mounts the same file and sets its own path.
HURON_CONFIG_FILE=huron.dev.yaml
